{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6385498","formula":"C₁₄H₁₈N₂O₅","hill":"C14H18N2O5","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":18.0,"N":2.0,"O":5.0},"names":{"en":"Kelatorphan"},"descriptions":{"en":"Kelatorphan is a drug which acts as a powerful and complete inhibitor of nearly all of the enzymes responsible for catabolism of the endogenous enkephalins, including neutral endopeptidase (NEP), dipeptidyl peptidase III (DPP3), aminopeptidase N (APN), and angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE). In mice, with the intracerebroventricular co-administration of a 50 μg dose of kelatorphan (this route is necessary because kelatorphan is incapable of crossing the blood-brain-barrier) hence alongside exogenous [Met]enkephalin (ED50 approximately 10 ng), it potentiated the analgesic effects of the latter by 50,000 times."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":123982,"mass":294.3,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@@H](C(=O)O)NC(=O)[C@H](CC1=CC=CC=C1)CC(=O)NO","inchikey":"OJCFZTVYDSKXNM-GXSJLCMTSA-N","iupac":"(2S)-2-[[(2R)-2-benzyl-4-(hydroxyamino)-4-oxobutanoyl]amino]propanoic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"123982","atoms":39,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.85,"y":0.124,"z":2.171,"el":"O"},{"x":3.701,"y":-0.868,"z":0.685,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.762,"y":2.734,"z":-1.424,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.124,"y":4.564,"z":-0.259,"el":"O"},{"x":4.392,"y":-1.373,"z":-1.876,"el":"O"},{"x":0.593,"y":1.04,"z":0.053,"el":"N"},{"x":3.221,"y":-1.906,"z":-1.319,"el":"N"},{"x":0.441,"y":-1.369,"z":0.302,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.828,"y":-2.047,"z":0.863,"el":"C"},{"x":1.704,"y":-2.229,"z":0.51,"el":"C"},{"x":0.647,"y":-0.004,"z":0.966,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.115,"y":-1.473,"z":0.326,"el":"C"},{"x":0.773,"y":2.426,"z":0.423,"el":"C"},{"x":2.977,"y":-1.578,"z":-0.007,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.719,"y":-0.417,"z":0.992,"el":"C"